(D2b — Discrepancy 2 repro (assembly-failure half): on 0.4.9 and earlier,
 the same map-parameter property read, in a program with no float in it,
 did not assemble — `symbol '_file_size' not defined`. That symbol name
 was the evidence for what D2 was: a map parameter's size/length compiled
 into the FILE size routine. A float elsewhere in the program linked the
 file runtime in, at which point the call resolved and silently returned
 -1 (the file-size error value) instead of failing to build.
 RESOLVED, 2026-08-22 — vox #76, same fix as D2 (see D2.vox). Re-run
 verbatim against 0.4.10: this program — no float anywhere in it — now
 assembles and links cleanly and prints the correct entry count.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D2b.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   2
)
